.TH "PB-TUNNEL-CONNECTOR-DRAIN" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-tunnel-connector-drain - Drain a tunnel connector


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb tunnel connector drain <tunnel> <connector> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Drain a tunnel connector

.PP
Stop assigning new work to one connector and optionally wait for existing work to finish. --timeout bounds the wait; the connector remains distinct from a revoked one.

.PP
Connectors attach an enrolled host to a durable tunnel. Drain stops new work while allowing existing work to wind down; revoke removes connector authority. Inspect connector state before replacing or removing one.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for drain

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print canonical JSON

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=2m0s
	maximum time to wait for operation completion

.PP
\fB--wait\fP[=false]
	wait for the operation to reach a terminal state


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--ephemeral\fP[=false]
	use the temporary preview lifecycle

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


